WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.792 --> 00:00:09.000
A lot of times,
when I choreograph,

00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:11.167
I had to look
at the environment

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.167
and that kind of sparks,

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.583
you know, what
we're going to do in there.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:16.667
The ramen stand

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.458
that she's eating
in the beginning,

00:00:18.542 --> 00:00:20.917
I mean, that thing
wasn't designed to...

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.833
we never thought
someone's gonna fall,

00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:25.917
like clip at the top of it
and fall down to the ground.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.917
So, we thought about it
and go, oh wow,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.250
we can maybe
have the gangsters

00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:32.750
try to come from all levels,

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:35.917
top floor, bottom floor,
so just to make it busy.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.917
I just wanted
to make it multi-level.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.583
So, we actually
had a stunt guy,

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.625
she shoots him,
he falls out the window,

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:46.542
rolls from the other roof
onto the top of the stand

00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:47.792
and then onto the ground.

00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:50.667
So, we had to reinforce it,
move the stand closer,

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.708
so I know
it's physically possible

00:00:52.792 --> 00:00:54.125
to clip it.

00:00:54.208 --> 00:00:56.667
And so, it always hurts,
but you know,

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.875
so they don't really
get seriously injured.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.417
All right, so that's one.
A lot of another thing too

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.667
was we have Mary running
up to the second floor

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.208
and we made the path
go to second floor.

00:01:07.292 --> 00:01:08.792
Then I'm like, okay,
she's not going to go back

00:01:08.875 --> 00:01:11.250
to the first floor,
she's going to...

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:14.667
we had to run down
this side of the roof

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.292
and we had to kinda
build that

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.083
where she could run
on top of it

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:20.042
and it's structural,
all right.

00:01:20.125 --> 00:01:21.167
And at the same time,

00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:23.333
because she's running
at a height,

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:24.542
we had to figure out, okay,

00:01:24.625 --> 00:01:26.750
we've gotta put
a wire system

00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:29.167
and a wire assist,
so she can kinda jump

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.167
from one rooftop
to the other.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.083
It's just interesting
to see those.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:34.958
Like once you get
in the environment,

00:01:35.042 --> 00:01:37.792
just a lot of the stuff
just changes

00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:39.042
and just gets bigger.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.875
When she runs
into the bathhouse,

00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:45.333
we entered a bathhouse
in Thailand

00:01:45.417 --> 00:01:48.208
and the actual bathhouse
was in Japan, right.

00:01:48.292 --> 00:01:50.792
And then when she runs out,
she's back in Thailand,

00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:53.292
I think what was interesting
about that piece is

00:01:53.375 --> 00:01:54.875
once she goes
into the bathhouse,

00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:55.917
that's real Japan.

00:01:57.375 --> 00:01:59.208
There's a rhythm
when you do the action

00:01:59.292 --> 00:02:02.000
because I think if you make
everything at 100%

00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:03.292
all the way through,

00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:04.833
people get
desensitised to it.

00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:07.417
So, you want to make
peaks and valleys

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.292
in terms of emotional arcs

00:02:09.375 --> 00:02:11.792
or rhythm when you do
these fight scenes.

00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:15.458
So, you want to start off
with tension

00:02:15.542 --> 00:02:16.792
and then it goes fast

00:02:16.875 --> 00:02:19.167
and then
there's a moment of levity.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.125
Got to find that.

00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:22.750
It's almost
like physical language.

00:02:22.833 --> 00:02:25.208
Call it physical language.
So, it's a scene,

00:02:25.292 --> 00:02:26.708
but everything's done
physically.

00:02:26.792 --> 00:02:28.917
So, you still
have to have those peaks

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.625
and arcs of emotion
throughout the fight.

00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:36.583
Otherwise, it's just
a big blur of movement

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:40.542
and I think people

00:02:40.625 --> 00:02:43.958
tend to need
a little moment of levity

00:02:44.042 --> 00:02:47.000
where everything slows down
so they can ingest it.

00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:54.958
She's doing
super-long takes.

00:02:55.042 --> 00:02:56.542
So, she's running
up and down,

00:02:56.625 --> 00:02:58.958
running up these stairs
doing all these things,

00:02:59.042 --> 00:03:02.000
so it's just a multitude
of things she had to do.

00:03:02.083 --> 00:03:03.833
And it's really hot
over there,

00:03:04.375 --> 00:03:07.417
so at night it's humid,
it's really hot,

00:03:07.917 --> 00:03:09.667
they're all wearing
long sleeved shirts

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.458
and pants
and things like that,

00:03:11.542 --> 00:03:14.167
but she's just doing
long takes

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.250
and she's doing everything.

00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:18.625
So, I can't really say

00:03:18.708 --> 00:03:20.875
what one thing
is harder than the other.

00:03:20.958 --> 00:03:23.083
I just think
it's just compounding

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:24.917
all that stuff onto her.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.875
It's a lot. But she does it.

